window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["dl-01.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">دليل المحور الأمامي (للدفع الرباعي): وصف الأجزاء بأرقامها، وإجراءات الضبط: الشدّ المسبق لبيرنكات البنيون والتفاضلي، وعمق البنيون وحساب الشيمات، وقياس Backlash.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> استعمله عند تبديل التروس أو البيرنكات. الضبط بالشيمات دقيق ويحتاج أدوات قياس، فاتبع الخطوات بالترتيب.</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">OVERVIEW</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">DRIVELINE/AXLES</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DESCRIPTION</strong><small>الوصف</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">1 - PINION HOUSING ASSEMBLY 7 - RING GEAR 2 - SHIM, PINION DEPTH 8 - COVER, AXLE 3 - O-RING SEAL, PINION HOUSING 9 - BEARING, DIFFERENTIAL SIDE (SMALL) 4 - BEARING, DIFFERENTIAL SIDE (LARGE) 10 - GEAR, PINION 5 - SHIM, SELECT 11 - BEARING, PINION HEAD 6 - DIFFERENTIAL ASSEMBLY 12 - BEARING, PINION TAIL</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The 175MM FIA (Front Independent Aluminum). is an independent assembly with an aluminum housing and cast iron differential. The 175MM FIA uses an open differential which is supported by two tapered roller bearings located on either side of the case. Differential bearing preload and ring gear backlash are controlled with select shims located on the outside of the differential bearing cups. Pinion height is set with a select shim sandwiched between the pinion housing assembly and the axle housing.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">1 - NUT, PINION FLANGE1 15 - BAFFLE, VENT 2 - FLANGE, PINION 16 - SEAL, AXLE 3 - SEAL, PINION 17 - SHIM, PRELOAD 4 - BEARING, PINION TAIL 18 - BEARING, DIFFERENTIAL SIDE 5 - BOLT, PINION HOUSING 19 - ASSEMBLY, RING GEAR/DIFFERENTIAL 6 - HOUSING, PINION 20 - BEARING, DIFFERENTIAL SIDE 7 - SPACER, SELECT 21 - SEAL, AXLE COVER O-RING 8 - BEARING, PINION HEAD 22 - SHIM, BEARING PRELOAD 9 - SEAL, PINION HOUSING O-RING 23 - COVER, AXLE HOUSING 10 - GEAR, PINION 24 - BOLT, AXLE HOUSING COVER 11 - SHIM, PINION DEPTH (SELECT) 25 - SEAL, AXLE 12 - HOUSING, AXLE 26 - PLUG, AXLE FILL 13 - VENT, HOUSING 27 - SHAFT, DIFFERENTIAL PINION 14 - HOUSING, AXLE 28 - SIDE GEAR ASSEMBLY</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The 175MM FIA Axle is available only in All-Wheel Drive models, and only in a 3:07:1 ratio.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ADJUSTMENTS</strong><small>الضبط</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">BEARING PRELOAD</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">PINION BEARING PRELOAD</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Pinion bearing preload is controlled and adjusted by means of a select- thickness spacer sandwiched between the pinion head and tail bearing cones.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove pinion housing bolts (1) and remove pinion housing assembly from axle housing.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a dial-type torque wrench (1), measure pinion housing rotating torque. Rotating torque should be within 130-260 N.m (12-23 in. lbs.). If rotating torque is below this range, disassemble pinion housing, measure and install a slightly thinner spacer (1), reassemble and reverify. If rotating torque is above this</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">range, disassemble pinion housing, install a slightly thicker spacer, reassemble and reverify rotating torque.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using Spanner Wrench (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) (2), remove pinion flange nut.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using Puller (special tool #1026, Puller) (1), remove pinion flange.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Press pinion gear (2) out of housing.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove pinion bearing preload spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Measure spacer (1) and correct per rotating torque measurement.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Install proper pinion bearing preload spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Install pinion gear/bearing assembly to housing. Using Installer (special tool #L-4507, Installer, Bearing) (1), press pinion tail bearing (2) onto shaft until it bottoms.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Using Installer (special tool #L-4507, Installer, Bearing) (1), press on pinion flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install the pinion flange nut and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Install pinion housing assembly and depth shim to axle assembly.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Install the pinion housing-to-axle housing bolts (1) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIFFERENTIAL SIDE BEARING PRELOAD</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Differential side bearing preload is controlled and adjusted by means of select- thickness shims sandwiched between the side bearing cups and the housing/cover.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          For accurate results, differential side bearing preload must only be measured when the pinion housing assembly is removed from the axle.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove pinion housing-to-axle housing bolts (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove pinion housing and depth shim (1) from axle assembly.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install Torque Tool (special tool #C-4995A, Tool, Differential Bearing Torque) (1) to differential housing as shown. Measure and record differential rotating torque. Differential rotating torque should be within 190-260 N.m (17-23 in. lbs.). If rotating torque is below this range, disassemble housing, measure and install slightly thicker preload shims (1). Add thickness equally to both sides. If rotating torque is above this range, disassemble housing, measure and install slightly thinner preload shims. Remove thickness equally from both sides.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove axle housing cover (5) and differential assembly (3).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove differential side bearing cup from axle housing cover. Install Bearing Remover (special tool #6514, Remover, Bearing Cup) (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove differential side bearing cup with Bearing Remover (special tool #6514, Remover, Bearing Cup) (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove side bearing preload shim (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Measure preload shim (1) to identify for replacement.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Install new differential side bearing preload shim (1) into axle housing cover (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Using Handle (special tool #C-4171, Driver Handle, Universal) and Installer (special tool #D-129, Installer, Bearing Cup) press new side bearing cup into cover until it bottoms. Use suitable cup (3) to support and protect cover.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Using Remover (special tool #9664, Remover, Bearing Cup) (1) and Slide Hammer (special tool #C-637, Slide Hammer, Universal) (2), remove differential side bearing (inboard) cup.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Measure preload shim (1) to identify for replacement.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Install new differential side bearing preload shim (1) into axle housing.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Using Handle (special tool #C-4171, Driver Handle, Universal) and Installer (special tool #D-145, Installer, Bearing Cup), press differential side bearing cup into housing until it bottoms.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Install differential/ring gear assembly (3), new cover o-ring seal (4), and cover (5).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Install the cover-to-housing bolts and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Again verify rotating torque measurement (1). Repeat adjustment procedure until proper rotating torque is obtained.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Install pinion housing assembly and depth shim (1). Use new o-ring on housing.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>Install the pinion housing-to-axle housing bolts (1) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">PINION DEPTH</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">PINION DEPTH VARIANCE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Identifying numbers for the ring gear and pinion are marked on the pinion (1). A plus (+) number, minus (-) number or zero (0). The pinion depth variance/deviation (1) is the amount the depth varies from the standard depth setting of a pinion marked with a (0). The standard depth provides the best gear tooth contact pattern.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The pinion depth is set by selecting the shim (1) that fits between the pinion housing and the axle housing. er</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">PINION DEPTH MEASUREMENT</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Install arbor disc (special tool #9681-4, Disc, Arbor) (1) into differential cover (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install arbor disc (special tool #9681-5, Disc, Arbor) (1) into differential case.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install arbor bar (special tool #D-115-3, Arbor) (1) into arbor disc (special tool #9681-5, Disc, Arbor).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install O-rings (1) on arbor bar (special tool #D-115-3, Arbor).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Install cover (1) to housing.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install the cover-to-housing bolts and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure gauge plate surfaces are clean to insure an accurate reading</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Install gauge plate (special tool #9681-2, Plate, Gage) (1) to pinion opening.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Install plate-to-housing bolts (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Install Scooter Block (2) and dial Indicator (1) on gauge plate (special tool #9681-2, Plate, Gage) (3).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Zero dial indicator (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Take reading (1) with the dial indicator, measure gage rod protrusion.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Record gage rod protrusion reading on the dial indicator. The dial indicator reading represents the amount that this particular assembly deviates from the design height.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">PINION ASSEMBLY HEIGHT MEASUREMENT</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Install measuring sleeve (special tool #9681-1, Gauge, Pinion Height) (1) over pinion assembly (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install Scooter Block (2) and dial Indicator on (1) measuring sleeve (special tool #9681-1, Gauge, Pinion Height) (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Record reading on the dial indicator. The dial indicator reading represents the amount that this particular assembly deviates from the design height.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SHIM CALCULATION</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">By adding the sum of the above readings you will be able to determine the correct shim needed.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Your base line shim will be 2.047 mm, add this to the pinion depth variance/deviation (1). The variance/deviation marking on the pinion head in 0.01 mm increments. Therefore, for the graphic shown, 0.03 mm (0.0012 in.) would be added to the shim thickness.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Add your dial indicator reading measurement for pinion height (1).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Add your gage rod protrusion measurement (1).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The sum of the above will be the shim size needed (1).</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">MEASURING BACKLASH</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use Backlash Tool (special tool #9682, Backlash Measuring Tool) (1) to check backlash.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install Backlash Tool (special tool #9682, Backlash Measuring Tool) (1) into the side gear and tighten the</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">lock down nut.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install Dial Indicator (special tool #C-3339A, Set, Dial Indicator) (2) to the differential cover and align the measuring tip of the Dial Indicator with the line on Backlash Tool (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Zero the Dial Indicator.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>While holding the pinion flange, rock the measuring arm back and forth stop - to - stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Record the reading on the Dial Indicator.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>To bring backlash with in specifications, subtract from one side and add equal amount of cup shims to the other side of the differential case and the differential cover as needed. (1.34-2.98 mm (0.053-0.117 in.) Available in 0.04 mm (0.0015 in.) increments).</span></div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS</strong><small>عزوم الشد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">GENERAL SPECIFICATIONS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><pre class=\"en-pre\">          DESCRIPTION                                          SPECIFICATION\n             Axle Ratio                                               3.07\n        Ring Gear Diameter                                      175 mm (6.9 in.)\n        Ring Gear Backlash                               0.05-0.11 mm (0.002-0.004 in.)\n    Differential Torque-to-Rotate                         190-260 N.cm (17-23 in. lbs.)\n  Pinion Housing Torque-to-Rotate                         130-260 N.cm (12-23 in. lbs.)\n                                              1.15-2.11mm (0.045-0.083 in.) Available in 0.04 mm\n      Pinion Depth Shim Size\n                                                             (0.0015 in.) increments\n                                                9.60-10.59mm (0.378-0.417 in.) Available in 0.03\n Pinion Bearing Preload Spacer Size\n                                                           mm (0.001 in.) increments</pre><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">DESCRIPTION                                    SPECIFICATION 1.31-2.51 mm (0.051-0.099 in.) Available in 0.04 Differential Bearing Preload Shim Size mm (0.0015 in.) increments 1.34-2.98 mm (0.053-0.117 in.) Available in 0.04 Differential Backlash Shim Size mm (0.0015 in.) increments</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS</strong><small>عزوم الشد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><pre class=\"en-pre\">         DESCRIPTION                       N.m         Ft. Lbs.   In. Lbs.        COMMENT\nAxle Assembly Support Bracket\n                                           28            21           -                 \nBolts\nAxle Cover-to-Housing Bolts\n                                           65            48           -                 \n(M10x40)\nAxle Cover-to-Housing Bolts\n                                           34            25           -                 \n(M8x25)\nAxle Housing Fill Plug                  30           22               -                 \nAxle Housing-to-Engine Bolts            65           48               -                 \nFront Pinion Flange Nut              475 +/- 25   360 +/- 18          -                 \nIntermediate Shaft-to-Engine Bolts      25           19               -                 \nPinion Housing-to-Axle Housing\n                                           34            25           -                 \nBolts</pre></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Raise and support the vehicle. Refer to HOISTING, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove both front half shafts. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove the front axle disconnect assembly. Refer to DISCONNECT, FRONT AXLE, REMOVAL.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the front propeller shaft. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove the Right Hand (RH) catalytic converter/exhaust pipe assembly. Refer to CONVERTER, CATALYTIC, REMOVAL .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Separate the power steering return line (3) from the cradle by unfastening the clips (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove the front axle housing support bracket (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Remove the seven front axle housing-to-engine bolts. Remove the front axle assembly (1) from vehicle.</span></div></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">WITH ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Position the front wheels in the straight ahead position and secure steering wheel to prevent it from turning.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the air cleaner body. Refer to BODY, AIR CLEANER, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Raise and support the vehicle. Refer to HOISTING, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove both front half shafts. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           It is not necessary to completely remove the front axle disconnect assembly from the vehicle.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Disconnect the front axle disconnect harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove the front axle disconnect assembly bolts. Refer to DISCONNECT, FRONT AXLE, REMOVAL.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Position the front axle disconnect and intermediate shaft to the left side enough to disengage from the front differential.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Mark the front propeller shaft to front axle flange for reassembly indexing.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove front propeller shaft from the front axle and position aside. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Remove the left and right side steering gear heat shield fasteners.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Remove RH catalytic converter/exhaust pipe assembly. Refer to CONVERTER, CATALYTIC, REMOVAL .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove lower intermediate shaft pinch bolt (2) at steering gear (3). Separate lower intermediate shaft (1) from steering gear (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Disconnect the two black steering gear wire harness connectors (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do NOT allow the steering gear to hang unsupported by the tie rods.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Position a suitable support under the steering gear and remove the steering gear to cradle bolts and nuts (3) with heat shield above each inner tie rod bellows.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Remove the two transmission case to crossmember bolts (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Using a suitable jack, raise the transmission.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Remove front axle housing support bracket (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Remove the seven front axle assembly-to-oil pan bolts. Remove axle assembly (1) from vehicle by rotating the axle counterclockwise for clearance while taking it out over the front suspension cradle.</span></div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DISASSEMBLY</strong><small>التفكيك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">1 - NUT, PINION FLANGE1 15 - BAFFLE, VENT 2 - FLANGE, PINION 16 - SEAL, AXLE 3 - SEAL, PINION 17 - SHIM, PRELOAD 4 - BEARING, PINION TAIL 18 - BEARING, DIFFERENTIAL SIDE 5 - BOLT, PINION HOUSING 19 - ASSEMBLY, RING GEAR/DIFFERENTIAL 6 - HOUSING, PINION</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">20 - BEARING, DIFFERENTIAL SIDE 7 - SPACER, SELECT 21 - SEAL, AXLE COVER O-RING 8 - BEARING, PINION HEAD 22 - SHIM, BEARING PRELOAD 9 - SEAL, PINION HOUSING O-RING 23 - COVER, AXLE HOUSING 10 - GEAR, PINION 24 - BOLT, AXLE HOUSING COVER 11 - SHIM, PINION DEPTH (SELECT) 25 - SEAL, AXLE 12 - HOUSING, AXLE 26 - PLUG, AXLE FILL 13 - VENT, HOUSING 27 - SHAFT, DIFFERENTIAL PINION 14 - HOUSING, AXLE 28 - SIDE GEAR ASSEMBLY</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove pinion housing assembly bolts (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove pinion housing assembly (4).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove pinion depth shim (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure pinion housing assembly rotating torque (1). Rotating torque should be 130-250 N.cm (12-22 in. lbs.). If rotating torque is outside of this range, bearing replacement is required. Refer to Pinion Housing Disassembly.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove pinion flange nut (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Using puller (special tool #1026, Puller) (1), pull pinion flange from shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove pinion flange (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Using suitable tool, remove pinion seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove pinion housing O-ring seal (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Measure differential rotating torque with Torque Tool C-4995A. Rotating torque should be within 190-250 N.cm (17-22 in. lbs). Measurements recorded out of this range require differential side bearing replacement and/or side bearing preload adjustment.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Remove axle housing cover (5). Remove differential assembly (3) and inboard axle seal (2).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove axle housing cover o-ring (1).</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ASSEMBLY</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">1 - NUT, PINION FLANGE1 15 - BAFFLE, VENT 2 - FLANGE, PINION 16 - SEAL, AXLE 3 - SEAL, PINION 17 - SHIM, PRELOAD 4 - BEARING, PINION TAIL 18 - BEARING, DIFFERENTIAL SIDE 5 - BOLT, PINION HOUSING 19 - ASSEMBLY, RING GEAR/DIFFERENTIAL 6 - HOUSING, PINION 20 - BEARING, DIFFERENTIAL SIDE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">7 - SPACER, SELECT 21 - SEAL, AXLE COVER O-RING 8 - BEARING, PINION HEAD 22 - SHIM, BEARING PRELOAD 9 - SEAL, PINION HOUSING O-RING 23 - COVER, AXLE HOUSING 10 - GEAR, PINION 24 - BOLT, AXLE HOUSING COVER 11 - SHIM, PINION DEPTH (SELECT) 25 - SEAL, AXLE 12 - HOUSING, AXLE 26 - PLUG, AXLE FILL 13 - VENT, HOUSING 27 - SHAFT, DIFFERENTIAL PINION 14 - HOUSING, AXLE 28 - SIDE GEAR ASSEMBLY</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">WITHOUT ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Install the front axle assembly (1) into position. Install and tighten the axle housing-to-engine bolts to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install power steering return line to cradle by fastening clips (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install axle assembly support bracket (1) and bolts and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the front axle disconnect. Refer to DISCONNECT, FRONT AXLE, INSTALLATION.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Install RH catalytic converter/exhaust pipe assembly. Refer to CONVERTER, CATALYTIC, INSTALLATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install front propeller shaft. Refer to INSTALLATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Install both front half shafts. Refer to HALF SHAFT, INSTALLATION . er</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Fill the axle with the specified fluid. Refer to CAPACITIES AND RECOMMENDED FLUIDS, SPECIFICATIONS . Fluid level should be at or near the bottom of the fill hole. Torque fill plug (1) to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove the support and lower the vehicle.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">WITH ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Install front axle assembly (1) into position. Install and tighten axle housing-to-engine bolts to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install axle assembly support bracket (1) and bolts and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Lower the transmission onto the crossmember.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the two transmission case to crossmember bolts (2) and tighten to the proper torque specifications.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Fill axle with 600ml (0.64 qts.) of Mopar® 75W-90 Synthetic Gear Lubricant. Fluid level should be at or near bottom of fill hole. Torque fill plug (1) to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Lift steering gear into mounted position and install steering gear to cradle bolts and nuts (3) with the heat shields, and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect the two black steering gear wiring harness connectors (2).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Align the lower intermediate shaft (1) to steering gear shaft (3). Install a NEW pinch bolt and tighten bolt to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Install the left and right side steering gear heat shield fasteners.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Install the front axle disconnect. Refer to DISCONNECT, FRONT AXLE, INSTALLATION.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install RH catalytic converter/exhaust pipe assembly. Refer to CONVERTER, CATALYTIC, INSTALLATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Install front propeller shaft. Refer to INSTALLATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Install both front half shafts. Refer to HALF SHAFT, INSTALLATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Lower vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Install the air cleaner body. Refer to BODY, AIR CLEANER, INSTALLATION .</span></div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SPECIAL TOOLS</strong><small>العدد الخاصة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">1026 - Puller (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9202, 9202A-CAN, 9202CC.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">1130 - Splitter, Bearing/Gear (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 6745, 6947, 6949, 9202, 9202A-CAN, 9202CC, 9299.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">6514 - Remover, Bearing Cup (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 6546.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">6958 - Wrench, Spanner (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 6947, 6949, 6966, 8204, 8204CC, 8667.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9664 - Remover, Bearing Cup (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9675, 9685, 9695.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9665 - Installer, Bearing (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9675, 9685, 9695.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9666 - Installer, Bearing (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9675, 9685, 9695.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9676 - Adapter Plug (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9675, 9685, 9695.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9677 - Installer, Seal (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9675, 9685, 9695.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9681-1 - Gauge, Pinion Height (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9674.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9681-2 - Plate, Gage (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9674.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9681-4 - Disc, Arbor (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9674.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9681-5 - Disc, Arbor (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9674.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">9682 - Backlash Measuring Tool (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9674.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">C-3339A - Set, Dial Indicator (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9202.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">C-4171 - Driver Handle, Universal (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9202, 9202A-CAN, 9202CC, 9299, 9299CC, 9299CC, 9300A-CAN.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">C-4995A - Tool, Differential Bearing Torque</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">C-637 - Slide Hammer, Universal (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9202.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">D-115-3 - Arbor (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 8667, 9516A-CAN.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">D-129 - Installer, Bearing Cup (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 6947, 6949, 8667.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">D-130 - Installer, Bearing Cup (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9695.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">D-145 - Installer, Bearing Cup (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 8667, 9695.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">L-4507 - Installer, Bearing (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9685, 9695.)</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DISCONNECT, FRONT AXLE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FRONT AXLE DISCONNECT (FAD) / INTERMEDIATE SHAFT ASSEMBLY</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The Front Axle Disconnect (FAD) / intermediate shaft is serviced only as a complete assembly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Raise and support the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the belly pan. Refer to BELLY PAN, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove left hand front half shaft assembly. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Front Axle Disconnect (FAD) actuator solenoid wire harness connector (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove the 3 bolts (5, 6, 7) from the FAD actuator solenoid, and remove the FAD actuator solenoid (8).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove the 3 bolts (1, 2, 3) from the FAD bracket, and remove the FAD bracket (4).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove the bolts (1, 2, 3, 4) from the FAD.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Remove the fasteners (1) from the front belly pan, on both sides, to allow access to the front cradle bolts.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Mark the rear of the cradle (1) on both sides by the rear bolts for installation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Support the cradle with jack stands (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Loosen the right hand front and rear cradle bolts (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove the left hand front and rear cradle bolts (1).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Lower the jack stands (1) and continue to support the cradle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Lower the left jack stand just below the cradle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Using a large pry bar (1), carefully pry down the front cradle (2) approximately 2 inches, and remove the FAD (3) from the vehicle.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FRONT AXLE DISCONNECT SOLENOID</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Raise and support the vehicle.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the front axle disconnect solenoid harness connector (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove the 3 bolts (5), (6), and (7) from the front axle disconnect solenoid (8).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the front axle disconnect solenoid (8).</span></div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FRONT AXLE DISCONNECT (FAD) / INTERMEDIATE SHAFT ASSEMBLY</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a large pry bar (1), carefully pry down the front cradle (2) approximately 2 inches, and install the Front Axle Disconnect (FAD) (3) in the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install the FAD-to-oil pan bolts (1, 2, 3, 4) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install the FAD actuator solenoid (8), and the 3 bolts (5, 6, 7) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the FAD bracket (4), the 3 bolts (1, 2, 3) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the FAD actuator solenoid wire harness connector (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install the left front half shaft assembly. Refer to HALF SHAFT, INSTALLATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Using the jack stands (1) raise the cradle enough to touch the frame.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Align the cradle by using the marks (1) made during removal.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Tighten the right hand front and rear cradle bolts (1) to the proper torque specifications. Refer to FRAME, TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Tighten the left hand front and rear cradle bolts (1) to the proper torque specifications. Refer to FRAME, TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install the front belly pan fasteners (1), both sides.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove the support and lower the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Verify the front end alignment is within specifications. Refer to WHEEL ALIGNMENT, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Install the belly pan. Refer to BELLY PAN, INSTALLATION .</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FRONT AXLE DISCONNECT SOLENOID</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Install the front axle disconnect solenoid (8), and the 3 bolts (5), (6), (7).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the front axle disconnect harness connector (1).</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FLUID</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">STANDARD PROCEDURE</strong><small>إجراء قياسي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FLUID FILL</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Raise and support the vehicle. Refer to HOISTING, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove axle fill plug (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Fill axle with 600ml (0.64 qts.) of Mopar® 75W-90 Synthetic Gear Lubricant. Fluid should be within 3/16&quot; of bottom of fill hole.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the axle fill plug and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">22</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SEAL, AXLE DRIVE SHAFT</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">23</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">RIGHT AXLE SEAL</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove right halfshaft assembly. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using suitable screwdriver, remove axle seal (1).</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">24</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">LEFT AXLE SEAL</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Inboard (Left) axle seal replacement requires removal and disassembly of the axle assembly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove front axle assembly. Refer to REMOVAL.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Drain the axle fluid by turning housing on its side and draining out of left output bore.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove differential cover (5) and differential (3). Remove and discard o-ring seal.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using (special tool #9664, Remover, Bearing Cup) and Slide Hammer (special tool #C-637, Slide Hammer, Universal), remove left axle seal.</span></div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">25</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">RIGHT AXLE SEAL</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using (special tool #C-4193A, Installer, Seal) (1), install new axle shaft seal.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install right halfshaft assembly. Refer to HALF SHAFT, INSTALLATION .</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">26</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">LEFT AXLE SEAL</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using Installer (special tool #L-4507, Installer, Bearing), install left (inboard) axle seal (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install differential (3). Install cover (5) with new o-ring seal (4).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install the cover-to-housing bolts and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the axle assembly into vehicle. Refer to INSTALLATION.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Fill the axle with the specified fluid. Refer to CAPACITIES AND RECOMMENDED FLUIDS, SPECIFICATIONS .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install the fill plug (1) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">27</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SEAL, PINION</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove propeller shaft and heat shield. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using Spanner Wrench (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) (2), remove pinion flange nut.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using Puller (special tool #1026, Puller) (1), remove pinion flange.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove pinion flange seal with suitable screwdriver and discard.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using (special tool #9677, Installer, Seal) (1), install a NEW pinion flange seal.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">er</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using Installer (special tool #L-4507, Installer, Bearing) (1), lightly tap pinion flange (2) onto the shaft, just enough to start the flange nut by hand.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install the pinion flange nut and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the propeller shaft and heat shield. Refer to INSTALLATION .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">er</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910419</p></div></div></details></div></details>";
